# f0 = the module, f3 = Message, f1 = readList, f2 = storeList
# `get: readList`: the half is a function declaration that another function names too, so it lives in a variable of the module, which nothing stores into again: the program's table says which function it holds (`initialization=Function function=f2 flags=[IsImmutable]`). The scan took a half only where the closure was made in the body itself, so Link listed the name on the prototype object without its halves.
# WHAT HUNG ON IT: the constructor stores `this.list = ..`, so the layout declares a field of the name. Link knew of no setter above, the walk laid that store into ONE guarded run with its neighbors, the guard "a store under the name passes by" never held (the accessor is there), and EVERY store of the run went by name at each construction.
